irac@yang.earlham.edu (Ira Carmel@Waycoolone) writes:

>Eating Tengu's works pretty well, but the way is works is a little tricky.
>If you have to teleport intrinsics and you eat a Tengu corpse you have a
>chance of gaining the intrinsic teleport. I think the chance is dependant on
>how fresh the corpse is (not sure about that). Then if you eat another you
>have a chance of gaining control. 
>	So to get teleport control intrinsic you must hang around with
>porting problems for awhile or have a ring of teleport controll in the middle.

I don't think this is quite right, since the other day I ate my first
tengu without any of the teleport intrinsics, and I got the message:
"You feel in control of yourself", indicating teleport control intrinsic
had been gained. This seems to be contrary to the spoiler file comments,
however, which claim you get intrinsics in the order listed.
Anyway, why waste good tengu corpses to get teleport. I always find that
enough leprechauns and nymphs turn up in the early levels to get
teleport from one of them. If they are asleep, don't attack them
outright (bad for luck), just kick a wall to wake them up.

